{"id":"word:hebrew:H6743","type":"word","title":"צָלַח","subtitle":"H6743 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to push forward, in various senses (literal or figurative, transitive or intransitive)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to צָלַח (H6743) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 65 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"צָלַח (tsâlach) means to push forward, in various senses (literal or figurative, transitive or intransitive) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 22 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"צָלַח","transliteration":"tsâlach","pronunciation":"tsaw-lakh'","strong":"H6743","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6743","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["וְ/הַצְלַ֔ח","וַ/תִּצְלַ֤ח","וַ/תִּצְלַ֨ח","תַצְלִֽיחוּ","וְ/הִצְלִ֣יחַ"],"morphs":[["HC/Vqw3fs",7],["HVqi3ms",7],["HC/Vhq3ms",5],["HVhrmsa",4],["HVhi2ms",3],["HC/Vhv2ms",3],["HVhi2mp",3],["HVqi3fs",3],["HVhi3ms",3],["HC/Vhw3ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to push forward, in various senses (literal or figurative, transitive or intransitive)","usage":"break out, come (mightily), go over, be good, be meet, be profitable, (cause to, effect, make to, send) prosper(-ity, -ous, -ously).","full":"H6743. tsalach I. [ צָלַח ] verb rush ; — (Thes and others compare צְלַח ᵑ7 , Syriac , cleave, penetrate , then advance , see following); — Qal Perfect 3feminine singular וְצָֽלְחָה consecutive 1Sam 10:6 ; 3 plural צָֽלְחוּ 2Sam 19:18 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִצְלַח Amos 5:6 (see below), 3 feminine singular וַתִּצְלַח Judg 14:6 +; — rush , ׳וְצ הַיַּרְדֵּן 2Sam 19:18 they rushed into the Jordan (dubious, see Dr HPS), ׳יִצ יוֺסֵף בֵּית כָּאֵשׁ Amos 5:6 lest he rush like fire upon the house of Joseph (or O house , etc. GASm; Now conjecture בָּאֵשׁ יַצִּית ); especially of sudden possession by ( אֱהִֹים ) י ׳רוּחַ , with עַל , with person Judg 14:6 the Spirit . . . rushed upon him, so 14:19 ; 15:14 ; 1Sam 10:6 , 10 ; 11:6 ; with אֶל person 16:13 and (of צ ׳רוּחַ רָעָה ) 18:10 . II. [ צָלַח צָלֵחַ, ] verb advance, prosper (Late Hebrew id. ; Phoenician Pi`el causative in proper name; Arabic be good condition , compare Sabean תצלךְ SabDenkm 93 ; Aramaic צְלַח , prosper ); — Qal Perfect 3feminine singular צָלֵ֑חָה Jer 12:1 ; Imperfect 3masculine singular יִצְלַח 13:7 +, etc.; Imperative masculine singular צְלַח ; — prosper , of way of wicked 12:1 compare Num 14:41 ; Isa 53:10 ; 54:17 ; Ezek 17:9-10 , Dan 11:27 ; with ל of thing, = be good for anything Jer 13:7 , 10 ; Ezek 15:4 ; subject person, absolute, Jer 22:30 , 20 ; Ezek 17:15 ; Psa 45:5 be successful ! לִמְלוּבָה וַתִּצְלְחִי Ezek 16:13 and thou didst prosper to royalty (dubious; strike out ᵐ5 Co Toy; &gt;Sta ZAW vi (1886), 337 f. Krae לִמְלָאכָה i.e. harlotry). Hiph`il Perfect 3masculine singular הִצְלִיחַ Gen 24:21 , 2 masculine singular וְהִצְלַחְתָּ֫ 1Chr 22:11 , etc.; Imperfect 3masculine singular יַצְלִיחַ Neh 2:20 +, וַיַּצְלַח 1Chr 29:23 ; 2Chr 32:30 , etc.; Imperative masculine singular הַצְלַח 1Kin 22:12 +, הַצְלִ֫יחָה Neh 1:11 , יִ֯חָ֫ה Psa 118:25 , etc.; Participle מַצְלִיחַ Gen 24:42 +; — 1 make prosperous, bring to successful issue , of ׳י , with accusative of man's way ( דֶּרֶךְ ), Gen 24:21 , 40 , 42 , 56 (J), with accusative of thing 39:3 , 23 (J), with accusative of person 2Chr 26:5 , with ל person Neh 1:11 ; 2:20 ; absolute send success Psa 118:25 ; human subject with accusative דֶּרֶךְ Deut 28:29 ; Josh 1:8 (D), Isa 48:15 ; Psa 37:7 , so probably 1:3 (al. below 2 ), 2Chr 7:11 ; with accusative מִרְמָה Dan 8:25 . 2 shew, experience, prosperity , of men 1Kin 22:12 , 15 2Chr 18:11 , 14 ; Jer 2:37 (+ ל person in reference to whom) 5:28 ; 32:5 ; 1Chr 22:11 , 13 ; 29:23 ; 2Chr 13:12 ; 14:6 ; 20:20 ; 24:20 ; 31:21 ; 32:30 ( בְּכָלמַֿעֲשֵׂהוּ ), Prov 28:13 ; Dan 8:12 (of horn), 8:24 ; 11:36 ; מַצְלִיחַ אִישׁ Gen 39:2 (J) a prosperous man ; subject דֶּרֶךְ Judg 18:5 (compare Psa 1:3 above), ׳י 's word Isa 55:11 . III. צלח (√ of following; Late Hebrew צְלֹחִית = Biblical Hebrew; compare Aramaic צְלוּחִיתָא , (in Lexicons) flat dish ; Ethiopic Amharic (see Prä Amh. Spr. § 65 c ); Arabic , all bowl, dish ; see Frä 63. 170 ). [ צְלַח ] verb prosper (see Biblical Hebrew II. צלח ); — Haph`el Perfect 3masculine singular הַצְלַח Dan 3:30 ; Daniel 6:29; Participle מַצְלַח Ezra 5:8 , plural לְחִין - 6:14 ; &#8212; 1 cause to prosper Dan 3:30 (with ל person). 2 shew prosperity, be prosperous Daniel 6:29 (of person); have success (in building) Ezra 6:14 ; be successful (of work) 5:8 ( בְּיֶדְהֹם ).","rootNote":"or צָלֵחַ ; a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 22 11","keyReferences":["1Chr 22 11","1Chr 22 13","1Chr 29 23","1Kgs 22 12","1Kgs 22 15","1Sam 10 6","1Sam 10 10","1Sam 11 6"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":65,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 22 11","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הִצְלַחְתָּ֗","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhq2ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 13","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תַּצְלִ֔יחַ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVhi2ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 23","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יַּצְלַ֑ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַצְלַ֔ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhv2ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 22 15","book":"1Kgs","chapter":22,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/הַצְלַ֔ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vhv2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 6","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/צָלְחָ֤ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq3fs"},{"reference":"1Sam 10 10","book":"1Sam","chapter":10,"verse":10,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/תִּצְלַ֤ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3f